  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "call_hierarchy",
  "title": "Function locals",
  "summary": "A function's local variables and parameters get no call hierarchy item",
  "prose": "The only function that can use them is the one declaring them, so an item\nfor them would have one caller, known in advance. A field of a class\ndeclared in a function keeps its item: the class's methods use it.",
  "status": "supported",
